From: Nex package maintainers
Subject: fips_enabled, hwf.deny, and random.conf readers walk the three UAPI tiers
Source: Nex downstream patch for libgcrypt 1.12.1
Upstream: not submitted; needs agreement on a machine-generated transient tier

libgcrypt hardwires three fixed-path readers of "/etc/gcrypt/" on Unix:
get_fips_force_file() in src/fips.c (checked with access(F_OK) from
check_fips_system_setting(), which also honors the LIBGCRYPT_FORCE_FIPS_MODE
environment variable as an unrelated, path-independent force flag),
get_hwf_deny_file() in src/hwfeatures.c (read with fopen() from
parse_hwf_deny_file(), called once from _gcry_detect_hw_features() before any
other thread runs), and get_random_conf_file() in random/random.c (read with
fopen() from _gcry_random_read_conf(), called from rndoldlinux.c and
rndjent.c). None of the three has a path override; only the FIPS force flag
above is unrelated to the file path. A full source sweep for other "/etc"
readers turns up only the legacy rndunix.c generator, which polls external
commands rather than reading files and is not compiled into this build
because glibc's getentropy() wins default random module selection in
configure.ac.

Each of the three get_*_file() helpers now walks /etc/gcrypt/<name>, then
/run/gcrypt/<name>, then /usr/lib/gcrypt/<name>, and returns the first path
that stat() reports as a regular file. A present higher-tier file masks a
lower one even if it is empty or only restates the compiled default, because
the walk stops at the first regular file, not the first file with content.
When no tier exists, every helper still returns the original
"/etc/gcrypt/<name>" path, so the original no-file behavior (access() or
fopen() failing on that exact path) is unchanged.

--- a/src/fips.c
+++ b/src/fips.c
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@
 #include <errno.h>
 #include <unistd.h>
 #include <string.h>
+#include <sys/stat.h>
 #ifdef ENABLE_HMAC_BINARY_CHECK
 # include <dlfcn.h>
 # include <elf.h>
@@ -137,7 +138,18 @@
     }
   return fname;
 #else
-  return "/etc/gcrypt/" FIPS_FORCE_FILE;
+  static const char *const tiers[] = {
+    "/etc/gcrypt/" FIPS_FORCE_FILE,
+    "/run/gcrypt/" FIPS_FORCE_FILE,
+    "/usr/lib/gcrypt/" FIPS_FORCE_FILE,
+  };
+  struct stat sb;
+  unsigned int i;
+
+  for (i = 0; i < sizeof (tiers) / sizeof (tiers[0]); i++)
+    if (stat (tiers[i], &sb) == 0 && S_ISREG (sb.st_mode))
+      return tiers[i];
+  return tiers[0];
 #endif
 }

